        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "North Star"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-00-overview-a-deterministic-run-sche-5": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-a-deterministic-run-sche-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A deterministic run scheduler understands the whole board. It admits bounded\ntarget packets to workers, then sleeps until durable state changes. Workers\nresearch, edit, verify, and report inside explicit leases. The system improves\nbecause each worker produces durable evidence, not because agents chat with each\nother or mutate source without accountability."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-00-overview-the-core-metaphor-is-sud-6": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-the-core-metaphor-is-sud-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The core metaphor is Sudoku: a worker may discover a fact or negative result\nthat does not finish its current target, but still constrains the board enough\nto make a different target the right next move."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-00-overview-the-runtime-can-also-be-7": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-the-runtime-can-also-be-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The runtime can also be wrapped by a guardian process for long-running\ndevelopment runs. That guardian watches system health events, records incidents,\nrecovers failed or expired leases, and restarts the decomp system process. It\ndoes not become a second scheduler."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
