    "b-00-overview-the-orchestrator-does-no-25": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-the-orchestrator-does-no-25",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The orchestrator does not own the compiler, objdiff, build system, or final PR\nreview. It wraps those tools and records their evidence. It also does not try to\nmaintain hidden, always-on agent memory. The board, not a long-lived chat\nthread, is the source of truth."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-00-overview-generated-state-belongs-26": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-generated-state-belongs-26",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Generated state belongs under an explicit state directory. The orchestrator is\nthe platform repo, and a selected project supplies the checkout root, state\ndirectory, graph database, process name, and local defaults. Runtime artifacts,\nSQLite files, prompts, and reports belong under the selected project's state\ndirectory unless an operator intentionally uses raw path overrides."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
